  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through Friday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Sat Jul 25 2026\n\nNot much to expound upon in the extended, which looks warm and dry, \nas the upper ridge doesn't move much.  Widespread triple digits are \nexpected each afternoon, with lows remaining unseasonably warm each \nnight due to the LLJ.  Tuesday now looks to be the warmest day this \nforecast, with high plateauing a good 8-10 F above normal.  However, \nthe rest of the days in the extended don't look more than a degree \nor two cooler, if that.  Heat Advisories creep back into the picture \nas soon as Monday, and continue all week.  Rain chances are \nnowhere to be found, and typical for late July.",
